mediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA, YOSHITERU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHARP KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBOI, HIDEKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMOTO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IMAMURA KIMIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA YOSHITERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBOI HIDEKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMOTO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IMAMURA, KIMIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA, YOSHITERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBOI, HIDEKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIMOTO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An OFDM receiver is provided with an offset compensating device (14) for compensating the frequency offset of a received OFDM signal. The offset compensating device (14) includes a memory (51) for holding two reference signals corresponding to arbitrary parts in the start symbol of the OFDM signal. The cross-correlation values between the received OFDM signal and the two reference signals are calculated by cross-correlation units (52 and 53), and respective peak positions are detected by a peak detector (54). A frequency offset estimate of the received OFDM signal is estimated by a frequency offset estimating circuit (55) based on the cross-correlation values in the detected peak positions. A phase rotating circuit (37) compensates the frequency offset of the received OFDM signal based on the estimated frequency offset estimate.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un récepteur OFDM doté d'un dispositif (14) de compensation de décalage, servant à la compensation du décalage de fréquence d'un signal OFDM. Le dispositif (14) de compensation du décalage comprend une mémoire (51) destinée à garder deux signaux de référence correspondant à des parties arbitraires du symbole de départ du signal OFDM. Les valeur de corrélation croisée entre le signal OFDM reçu et les deux signaux de référence sont calculées par des unités (52, 53) de corrélation croisée, un détecteur de crête (54) détectant les positions des crêtes respectives. Un circuit d'estimation (55) du décalage de fréquence estime le décalage de fréquence du signal OFDM reçu en fonction des valeurs de corrélation croisée aux positions des crêtes détectées. Un circuit de rotation de phase (37) compense le décalage de fréquence du signal OFDM reçu en fonction de l'estimation du décalage de fréquence.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>